## Steering — contiguous-window reformulation of Ψ(k) (asserted, unverified)

The operator redirected this run with a new claimed route (posted this cycle).
Asserted, **not yet verified in-container** — treat every claim below as a
hypothesis until a program (mech_psi/brute) confirms it.

- **Claim 1 (the key set identity).** For every n with F_n > k, the k+1
  DISTINCT length-k factors of the Fibonacci word are exactly the k+1
  CONTIGUOUS windows at positions r = F_n−k−1 .. F_n−1 of the doubled standard
  word q_n q_n. "As sets they are equal, every time."
- **Claim 2 (the computation).** Ψ(k) = (full cyclic sum over all F_n windows
  of q_n q_n) − (sum over the FIRST F_n−k−1 windows). I.e. Ψ(k) is a prefix
  partial sum of the window values v_r², no multiplicity, no dedup, no sum over
  O(k) intercepts.
- **Claim 3 (rehabilitates directive 1 for general k).** The full cyclic sum
  equals Σ_{j,jp} A(jp−j)·10^(2k−2−j−jp) with A the cyclic autocorrelation of
  q_n, for ANY k < F_n. Directive 1's identity was never restricted to
  k=F_n−1 as a statement about the CYCLIC sum; the restriction was only about
  the cyclic sum equalling Ψ. It does not in general; claim 2 is the
  correction term.
- **Algorithm.** v_(r+1) = 10·v_r − y_r·10^k + y_(r+k), y the Fibonacci word;
  carry (v, Σv², Σv, 1) as a constant-size transfer matrix whose step depends
  on the pair (y_r, y_(r+k)); collapse the product over the range by
  Fibonacci-block renormalisation — about 87 blocks at 10^18.
- **Worked check at k=3:** the five windows of q_4 q_4 = 0100101001 are
  010,100,001,010,101; the last four are the four distinct factors, and
  10000+1+100+10201 = 20302 = Ψ(3). ✓ (consistent with the problem's oracle)

